From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PANP2010 <18610364979@163.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 12:43:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nebula: fix getCurrentWorldData() NPE on coordinator thread
 for command-triggered async chunk-load callbacks

Root cause: /fill, /setblock etc. schedule async chunk loads whose onLoad
callback runs on the global coordinator thread during tickGlobal(), where no
region world-data context is installed, so getCurrentWorldData() returns null
and setBlock() NPEs deep in the call tree (captureTreeGeneration,
captureBlockStates, populating, pathTypesByPosCache, ...).

Primary fix: install the owning region's world-data context around the onLoad
callback in ServerLevel.moonrise$loadChunksAsync via new
TickRegionScheduler.nebula$pushWorldDataContext/restoreWorldDataContext +
RegionizedData.getForRegion(region).

Defense-in-depth: null-guard the worldData dereferences reachable from this
path in Level (getBlockState, getBlockStateIfLoaded, setBlock,
notifyAndUpdatePhysics, getBlockEntity, setBlockEntity, addBlockEntityTicker,
neighborShapeChanged, getRedstoneGameTime) and LevelChunk (setBlockState,
getBlockEntity, populate). Added Level.getWorldDataForPos for off-thread
position-resolved access.

